the new range rover sport since people  seldom actually take it off-road  land rover has concentrated on making  the vehicle better on the road itself  we'll be testing it here at a small  airfield in minor target  first sasha drives slalom through a  series of traffic cones  but before we test the chassis let's see  how the design has changed  the youngest generation of the range  rover sport has a powerful dynamic  appearance  compared with its predecessor its  wheelbase has increased by almost  18 centimeters and the car itself is  almost six centimeters longer  short overhangs improve the aerodynamics  the interior boasts well-crafted  high-quality materials  lots of carbon fiber polished aluminium  and  leather give the british car a sporty  luxurious look  and now the slalom through the traffic  cones the new range rover sport is built  entirely of aluminium  making it 420 kilograms lighter than its  predecessor  this radical diet means the suv runs  relatively dynamically and sportily on  the road  even though it still weighs more than  two tons  the air suspended chassis now has  stiffer bearings and larger stabilizers  a noticeable improvement when making  rapid maneuvers  the new range rover sport took the  obstacle course with such sporty dynamic  ease that sasha says its handling has  caught up with the porsche cayenne  and the bmw x5  the three liter diesel engine in our car  accelerates it from zero to 100  kilometers an hour in 7.2 seconds  the engine's 215 kilowatts give the suv  an electronically limited top speed of  210 kilometers an hour  the manufacturer rates its co2 emissions  at 199 grams per kilometer  that's high but acceptable when compared  with other suvs  a hybrid driven version is in the works  and expected to reduce fuel consumption  to 5 liters per 100 kilometers  we'll see  this is a range rover we've seen how the  range rover sport performs on the road  but now sasha wants to see what it can  do off-road  a little test track has been set up it  is very narrow  sasha shows how it damaged a previously  tested sports wheel rim  to avoid damaging the new car we'll use  the old ones  to stay on the safe side our tester has  brought in a professional  instructor thomas capelli he'll take the  car through the test track  explains that we'll deal with the  narrowness of the course by using the  camera system  the range rover sport has five cameras  the car can be guided with centimeter  close precision using the two outside  mirror cameras  that takes some getting used to but the  driver can see how the wheels respond  to every movement of the steering wheel  but the cameras give the driver complete  control  and good control is crucial when driving  off-road  patience and precision are how you avoid  damage  next comes a real test of the range  rover sports stamina  the heavy burden on the left front and  right rear  the left rear and right front bear  little or no weight  putting tremendous torsion and pressure  on the body  but that is all compensated and right  and left  front and back are all crosswise  decompressed  the wheels briefly spin the system  strain and the vehicle keeps moving  showing that it can manage off-road  conditions well as the instructor says  anyone can let a wheel drop half a meter  to hit the ground but it's nice when  that doesn't shake you up inside the car  the range rover sport is now available  from german dealers  for now three different engines are on  offer two diesels and a five liter v8  gasoline engine  sasha says the starting price of the new  range rover sport is 25 000 euros lower  than for its predecessor  down to 60 000 but if you want a v8  compressor engine  that will cost you 88 000 euros a few  extras soon put you over 100 000 euros  so  most people will have to think twice  about whether they can afford it  the third member of the lyon family the  new sea at leon st  combines dynamic design with precise  performance and  high use value the sports tourer comes  with a choice of two gasoline and three  diesel engines ranging from 63  to 135 kilowatts the chic  sports station wagon has it all comfort  fun driving and lots of room  it'll be available in europe from the  end of november  ford europe has offered an exclusive  glimpse of the future  for example further development of the  parking assistant means drivers can get  out and let their cars park themselves  using wireless technology cars can  exchange information about the traffic  situation  and warn each other of hazards ford has  also presented a system  for automatically avoiding obstacles  it's been a long time since golf gtis  had to buy with opal mantas for the  hearts of boy racers  only one of the two models has survived  and now it's fresher than ever  37 years after it was first introduced  volkswagen has unveiled its most  powerful gti to date  drive it tests the gti performance to  see just how much muscle  it really packs  the gti performance has 230 horsepower  and that gives it a 10 horsepower edge  over the standard gti says reviewer  there's fantastic acceleration and  pulling power  there's also an active limited slip  differential that makes a big difference  in traction  especially when cornering in short the  gti  is fun the 4-cylinder 2-liter petrol  engine is turbocharged for extra punch  it does 0-100 kilometers an hour in 6.4  seconds and produces a maximal torque of  350 newton meters  says that's one of many design elements  making this gti stand out from the  standard product  the characteristic rims aggressive sill  and the red lining in the radiator  grille all  add to the overall powerful effect the  many gti badges have  more to do with tradition  the gti passed the moose test with  flying colours thanks to its bite and  agility  the driver is in control all the time  here he needs only 34 meters breaking  space from 100 kilometers an hour  and it doesn't take him long to get back  up to speed either  the upholstery has the typical check  pattern with red stitching  it's exactly what you would expect from  a gti interior  as in the golf ball gear knob there's  plenty of space also in the trunk  the six gear manual shift did well on  the ecological front we measured fuel  consumption of 6.5 liters of super per  100 kilometers  although volkswagen claim only six  liters for the same distance  our findings mean 180 grams of co2 per  kilometer  and the clean exhaust wins additional  points for the car  the gti performance costs 29 825 euros  with manual shift  and brita says that's a fair price for a  car with such powerful performance  sporty design and extras it's your  decision  whether the gti image suits you  bmw added the gt to its upper medium  class 5 series in 2009  now the company has sold more than a  million of the sixth generation five  series  it's given the range a facelift the  improvements aren't just superficial  the gran turismo is more high-tech too  but  is it really a hatchback in the classic  sense  drive it tests the most extravagant 5  series model  bmw's frank emmanuel agrees that the  5-series gt  isn't necessarily comparable to the  hatchback limousines of the past  actually it takes the best of various  car types it's a four-door limousine  but like the x5 it has a raised seating  position which gives you a better  overview of the traffic and it's packed  into a coupe-like  elegant form  we're testing the 535ix drive the  smaller of the two petrol models on  offer  the six-cylinder engine produces a  maximum torque of 400 newton meters and  delivers 225 kilowatts of power  it's on sale for 62 300 euros in germany  the bottom of the range 135 kilowatt  diesel can be had for less than  50 000 euros  says the 5 series navigation system  comes with a touchpad  which recognizes letters as you trace  them with your finger  first choose destination and enter  a new destination  the computer  you can talk and keep your hands on the  wheel you drive and talk to someone as  if you were talking to someone next to  you  says the good thing about the 5-series  gran turismo is its versatility  you can move the rear seat back and  forward you can adjust the rear seat  armrest  and that all means there's a lot more  space in the trunk  in fact there's between 500 and 1700  liters of storage space  so at a pinch it has more space than the  5 series station wagon  bmw's frank emanuel says this is a car  conceived for long journeys like the  name says  gran turismo there's a lot of space in  the interior especially at the back  the materials used are high quality so  it offers quite a luxury setting  it's a car designed for a certain taste  and a particular kind of customer  so the number of vehicles produced is  naturally not very large  so it's a car for demanding and  extravagant customers  says the interior of the graniturismo is  a very different one from the normal 5  series  including the dashboard and the whole  front it's a lot more  curved the middle console is wider than  in the normal 5 series  there's an issue with being able to see  out the back  you can hardly see anything from the  front due to the rising shoulder line  and the narrow window at the rear  so parking backwards without a camera is  a challenge  there are things he likes and things he  doesn't like about the five series gran  turismo  just like with any other car he likes  the dashboard and the central console  and the way the car drives  he doesn't like the way it looks from  behind but then again  he can't see that when he's driving  is passionate about classic english  sports cars  here in a small back garage in munich is  his greatest treasure  an mgtc ten thousand of them were  originally produced  says that that's a relatively large  number of vehicles  they were built in various types and  versions but technically they were  basically the same  the car has four drum brakes situated  here  which have to be adjusted manually you  have to tinker around a bit  the front and back axles are attached  with leaf springs  that's a bit unstable and you notice it  on the curves  shows us where the tank and the spare  tires are at the back  he says the car has lever arm shock  absorbers which are typically  english and they need to be constantly  filled with oil  the mgtc was launched shortly after the  end of world war  ii and is the most spartan mg of the  t-series  with its long hood separate fenders low  doors and compact trunk  it looks like a classic 1930s english  roadster  describes the bodywork which is made of  wood and steel plating  the body shell is assembled around an  ash wood frame  he says even the door has an ash wood  frame with steel body panels nailed into  it  and then  enjoys every minute in the tc it only  weighs 820 kilograms  he's willing to put up with a bit of a  bumpy ride in exchange for a thrilling  driving experience  he says the joys of driving an mg tc are  having the wind blowing in your face  and the way you're in control of the  vehicle  there are no electronics and there's no  heating  you're really close to nature and have  the feeling that you're fighting the  elements  technical as well as natural elements  he says he's bored by modern cars  the direct steering takes some getting  used to and sometimes driving the tc  feels like riding a  bucking bronco  but he says he's got used to feeling the  uneven road surfaces  he just holds on tight and bumps along  you can reach speeds of up to 125  kilometers an hour with the 1250cc  engine it's good for 54 horsepower  back in his garage he checks the engine  compartment in the past it wasn't  possible to seal engines well  classic cars frequently suffer from  small oil leaks  says it's time to get the original oil  cap fixed so he's going to swap it for  his  bathtub plug in the meantime the plug  fits relatively well and  should seal it pretty well  began some 50 years ago  he says he first saw the mgtc in 1963  and was completely bowled over by the  shape of the car  the big 19-inch wheels and the  rectilinear form  he says it's a car that is rarely seen  on the road but still has a sporty look  found his mg in norway and spent a lot  of money and time restoring it  he drives the car almost every day when  the weather is pleasant and  sometimes even in winter too  it's important he's clocked up more than  500 000 kilometers in his mgtc  he says and has changed the pistons only  once  that for many people the car is not  suitable for everyday driving he says  is because it requires a lot of  attention the radiator has to be kept  full  and it's best to keep the car in a  garage  but if you have an aptitude for  tinkering around with cars the mgtc  can become a friend for life that was  the case for les brestida  and before him for stars like clark  gable and  formula one world champion phil hill  so  you

